  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coastal Protection Beira</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An investment in the coastal protection in the City of Beira, Mozambique following Cyclone Idai on 14 March 2019. The coastal protection of the City of Beira in Mozambique, which protects the livelihoods and assets in a large part of the city, has been damaged severely during this disaster.On 31 May and 1 June 2019 a donor conference was held in Beira to help rebuild areas and infrastructure destroyed by cyclones Idai and Kenneth. The Dutch government has pledged, amongst others, to further explore financial support through co-financing with the World Bank for rehabilitation of the coastal protection in Beira.</narrative>
  </description>
